# Unity regenerates all of this from Assets/ + Packages/ + ProjectSettings/ on open.
# None of it is source — don't commit it.

[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Mm]emoryCaptures/
[Rr]ecordings/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/

# Auto-generated per-IDE project/solution files. Unity rewrites these itself
# from the Assets folder every time the editor opens; hand edits don't survive.
*.csproj
*.sln
*.slnx
*.suo
*.tmp
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# Crash/build byproducts
sysinfo.txt
crashlytics-build.properties
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.app

# The repo's root .gitignore has a NuGet rule ("**/[Pp]ackages/*") that would
# otherwise also swallow Unity's Packages/ folder here. Re-include the two
# files that actually need to be committed — they pin your package versions.
!Packages/manifest.json
!Packages/packages-lock.json

# The root .gitignore also has a blanket "*.meta" rule (meant for an unrelated,
# much older VS convention) that would otherwise swallow every real Unity
# per-asset metadata file in this project. Those need to be committed — each
# one stores the GUID Unity uses to identify that asset, which scenes and
# prefabs reference directly; losing them lets Unity mint new GUIDs on the
# next reimport and silently breaks anything that pointed at the old ones.
!*.meta
!**/*.meta

# Assets/Brain is an NTFS junction to ../../Brain/src (Brain's real, tracked
# location). Git follows junctions when walking the tree, so without this it
# would see and commit every file in there a second time, under this alias
# path — meta files included, despite the re-include above. The junction only
# exists on disk for Unity's benefit; it has no git identity of its own.
Assets/Brain/
